-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDER 62: SECURITIES AND FUTURES ACT -- CIVIL PENALTY ACTIONS (12 rules): how the Monetary Authority of Singapore
-- sues for a civil penalty under the Securities and Futures Act (sections 137ZD, 232, 236B(3), 236C, 236E(3), 236F
-- and 236H), and how the ordinary Rules are changed for that kind of action.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  A MAYBE BOOLEAN answer is:
--   JUST TRUE   the text says yes on these facts.
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words (the FALSE-kind comment quotes them).
--   NOTHING     the text does not answer on these facts (the NOTHING-kind comment says why).
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- O 3 r 2(1) is a caveat on every answer: every requirement in the Rules is subject to the Court's
-- discretion to order otherwise in the interests of justice; it is not threaded as an input.
-- What follows non-compliance with a Rule is O 3 r 2(4); the functions below that say NOTHING for a "must"
-- not done cite that provision.
--
-- BORROWED FACTS.  The Securities and Futures Act is not among the sources.  Its sections are named in the
-- inputs and asked as facts; who is a "contravening person" in each proceeding is given by the Act (rule 1(1)),
-- and the encoding reports only which section gives the meaning.
-- Other Orders this Order applies or disapplies (Order 3 rule 2, Order 5, Order 6, Order 9, Order 10, Order 11,
-- Order 14, Order 21) are in other parts: what they say is not here (S-L1/S-L2), and a function that overrides
-- one is a flat statement about that provision and carries a FALSE-kind comment.
--
-- TIME.  O 3 r 3(1) says the Interpretation Act does not apply to the calculation of time in these Rules.
-- Whether an act was in time is a comparison with an input (seam S-T1: roc1's O 3 r 3 computes it, and the merged
-- file wires it).  The time limited for filing and serving a notice of intention to contest or not contest is O 6's
-- (seam: `o 6 r 6 the last day ...`), and so is the period fixed for service of the defence.

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 62 -- Securities and Futures Act, civil penalty actions`
-- ===========================================================================

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 1 -- definitions and application of this Order`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- The proceedings the Order speaks of, by the section of the Act under which each is brought.
DECLARE `o 62 r 1 proceeding` IS ONE OF
    `o 62 r 1 a proceeding under section 137ZD`
    `o 62 r 1 a proceeding under section 232`
    `o 62 r 1 a proceeding under section 236B(3)`
    `o 62 r 1 a proceeding under section 236C`
    `o 62 r 1 a proceeding under section 236E(3)`
    `o 62 r 1 a proceeding under section 236F`
    `o 62 r 1 a proceeding under section 236H`
    `o 62 r 1 a proceeding under another section`

-- src:7153 | 1. —(1) In this Order — “Act” means the Securities and Futures Act, and any reference to a section is a reference to a section in the Act;
@ref O 62 r 1(1) "Act" (src:7153)
`o 62 r 1(1) the Act` MEANS "the Securities and Futures Act"

-- "any reference to a section is a reference to a section in the Act".  The text carves out no reference that
-- names another Act expressly; it is silent on one.
-- src:7153 | 1. —(1) In this Order — “Act” means the Securities and Futures Act, and any reference to a section is a reference to a section in the Act;
@ref O 62 r 1(1) (src:7153)
GIVEN `the reference is to a section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reference names another Act expressly` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 62 r 1(1) a reference to a section is a reference to a section in the Act` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the reference names another Act expressly`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Rule does not say what a reference does that names another Act
        IF `the reference is to a section`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any reference to a section" speaks only of a reference to a section

-- src:7154 | “Authority” means the Monetary Authority of Singapore established by section 3 of the Monetary Authority of Singapore Act;
@ref O 62 r 1(1) "Authority" (src:7154)
`o 62 r 1(1) "Authority" who it is` MEANS "the Monetary Authority of Singapore established by section 3 of the Monetary Authority of Singapore Act"

-- "civil penalty action" means any proceeding commenced by the Authority under section 137ZD, 232, 236B(3), 236C,
-- 236E(3), 236F or 236H.  A "means" definition, so a case outside it is JUST FALSE.
-- src:7155 | “civil penalty action” means any proceeding commenced by the Authority under section 137ZD, 232, 236B(3), 236C, 236E(3), 236F or 236H;
@ref O 62 r 1(1) "civil penalty action" (src:7155)
GIVEN `the proceeding is commenced by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      proceeding IS A `o 62 r 1 proceeding`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 62 r 1(1) "civil penalty action" the proceeding is a civil penalty action` MEANS
    IF `the proceeding is commenced by the Authority` AND (NOT (proceeding EQUALS `o 62 r 1 a proceeding under another section`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means any proceeding commenced by the Authority under section 137ZD, 232, 236B(3), 236C, 236E(3), 236F or 236H"

-- src:7156 | “Code” means the Criminal Procedure Code;
@ref O 62 r 1(1) "Code" (src:7156)
`o 62 r 1(1) "Code" which Code` MEANS "the Criminal Procedure Code"

-- src:7157 | “Commercial Affairs Officer” means a Commercial Affairs Officer appointed under section 64 of the Police Force Act;
@ref O 62 r 1(1) "Commercial Affairs Officer" (src:7157)
GIVEN `the person is appointed under section 64 of the Police Force Act as a Commercial Affairs Officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 62 r 1(1) "Commercial Affairs Officer" the person is a Commercial Affairs Officer` MEANS
    IF `the person is appointed under section 64 of the Police Force Act as a Commercial Affairs Officer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a Commercial Affairs Officer appointed under section 64 of the Police Force Act"

-- "contravening person": the section that gives the meaning, by the proceeding.  The meaning itself is in the Act.
-- src:7158 | “contravening person” — ( a )
-- src:7159 | in relation to a proceeding under section 236B(3), has the meaning given by section 236B(1);
-- src:7160 | ( b )
-- src:7161 | in relation to a proceeding under section 236C, has the meaning given by section 236C(1);
-- src:7162 | ( c )
-- src:7163 | in relation to a proceeding under section 236E(3), has the meaning given by section 236E(1);
-- src:7164 | ( d )
-- src:7165 | in relation to a proceeding under section 236F, has the meaning given by section 236F(1); and
-- src:7166 | ( e )
-- src:7167 | in relation to a proceeding under section 236H, has the meaning given by section 236H(1);
-- src:7168 | “police officer” means a member of the Singapore Police Force who is deployed in the Commercial Affairs Department of that Force.
@ref O 62 r 1(1) "contravening person" (src:7158-7168)
GIVEN proceeding IS A `o 62 r 1 proceeding`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`o 62 r 1(1) "contravening person" the section that gives its meaning` MEANS
    CONSIDER proceeding
    WHEN `o 62 r 1 a proceeding under section 236B(3)` THEN JUST "section 236B(1)"
    WHEN `o 62 r 1 a proceeding under section 236C` THEN JUST "section 236C(1)"
    WHEN `o 62 r 1 a proceeding under section 236E(3)` THEN JUST "section 236E(1)"
    WHEN `o 62 r 1 a proceeding under section 236F` THEN JUST "section 236F(1)"
    WHEN `o 62 r 1 a proceeding under section 236H` THEN JUST "section 236H(1)"
    WHEN `o 62 r 1 a proceeding under section 137ZD` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): no limb of "contravening person" speaks of a proceeding under section 137ZD; QC: NOTHING (a bare list of limbs) / other: JUST FALSE (the definition is the list); a STRING cannot carry JUST FALSE, so the other reading would need a yes/no twin
    WHEN `o 62 r 1 a proceeding under section 232` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): no limb of "contravening person" speaks of a proceeding under section 232; QC as for section 137ZD
    WHEN `o 62 r 1 a proceeding under another section` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): no limb of "contravening person" speaks of a proceeding under any other section; QC as for section 137ZD

-- src:7168 | “police officer” means a member of the Singapore Police Force who is deployed in the Commercial Affairs Department of that Force.
@ref O 62 r 1(1) "police officer" (src:7168)
GIVEN `the person is a member of the Singapore Police Force deployed in the Commercial Affairs Department of that Force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 62 r 1(1) "police officer" the person is a police officer` MEANS
    IF `the person is a member of the Singapore Police Force deployed in the Commercial Affairs Department of that Force`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a member of the Singapore Police Force who is deployed in the Commercial Affairs Department of that Force"

-- Rule 1(2): the Rules apply to proceedings under the seven sections, "subject to the following Rules of this Order".
-- src:7169 | (2) These Rules apply to a proceeding commenced under section 137ZD, 232, 236B(3), 236C, 236E(3), 236F or 236H subject to the following Rules of this Order.
@ref O 62 r 1(2) (src:7169)
