§§ `Rule 2 -- commencement of civil penalty action, etc.`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:7171 | 2. —(1) A civil penalty action must be commenced by originating claim. (2) Order 6, Rules 2, 3 and 5 (other than Rule 5(3) and (4)) apply to a civil penalty action unless modified by this Rule.
@ref O 62 r 2(1) (src:7171)
GIVEN `the proceeding is a civil penalty action` IS A BOOLEAN
      document IS A `Document kind`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 62 r 2(1) the civil penalty action is commenced as the Rule requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the proceeding is a civil penalty action`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): rule 2(1) speaks of "A civil penalty action"
        IF document EQUALS `Originating claim`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a bare "must be commenced by originating claim"; QB: NOTHING (O 3 r 2(4)) / other: JUST FALSE

-- (2): "Order 6, Rules 2, 3 and 5 (other than Rule 5(3) and (4)) apply to a civil penalty action unless modified by this Rule."
-- src:7171 | 2. —(1) A civil penalty action must be commenced by originating claim. (2) Order 6, Rules 2, 3 and 5 (other than Rule 5(3) and (4)) apply to a civil penalty action unless modified by this Rule.
-- src:7172 | (3) The Authority must endorse on the originating claim — ( a )
@ref O 62 r 2(2) (src:7171-7172)
GIVEN `the proceeding is a civil penalty action` IS A BOOLEAN
      provision IS A STRING
      `rule 2 modifies the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 62 r 2(2) the provision applies to the civil penalty action` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the proceeding is a civil penalty action`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): rule 2(2) speaks of "a civil penalty action"
        IF elem provision (LIST
            "Order 6 rule 5(3)",
            "Order 6 rule 5(4)")
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(other than Rule 5(3) and (4))" limits the grant; QE: NOTHING (the parenthesis limits the grant "apply" and does not say that Rule 5(3) and (4) do not apply) / other: JUST FALSE (read as "except": Order 6, Rule 5(3) and (4) do not apply to a civil penalty action)
        IF NOT (elem provision (LIST
            "Order 6 rule 2",
            "Order 6 rule 3",
            "Order 6 rule 5"))
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): only "Order 6, Rules 2, 3 and 5" are named
        IF `rule 2 modifies the provision`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless modified by this Rule"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (3): what the Authority must endorse on the originating claim.
DECLARE `o 62 r 2(3) endorsement` HAS
    `o 62 r 2(3)(a) states the provision of the Act contravened by the defendant or under which the defendant is liable for the payment of a civil penalty` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 62 r 2(3)(b) states the address of the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 62 r 2(3)(b) the Authority sues by a solicitor` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 62 r 2(3)(b) states the solicitor's name or firm and a business address of the solicitor` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 62 r 2(3)(c) a defendant is sued in a representative capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 62 r 2(3)(c) states the capacity in which the defendant is sued` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 62 r 2(3)(d) states the number of days within which a notice of intention to contest or not contest is to be filed and served` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 62 r 2(3)(e) a statement of claim is endorsed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 62 r 2(3)(e) a concise statement of the nature of the claim or the relief or remedy required is endorsed` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:7172 | (3) The Authority must endorse on the originating claim — ( a )
-- src:7173 | a statement of the provision of the Act contravened by the defendant or under which the defendant is liable for the payment of a civil penalty, as the case may be;
-- src:7174 | ( b )
-- src:7175 | the address of the Authority or, if the Authority sues by a solicitor, the Authority’s address and the solicitor’s name or firm and a business address of the solicitor;
-- src:7176 | ( c )
-- src:7177 | where a defendant is sued in a representative capacity, a statement of the capacity in which the defendant is sued;
-- src:7178 | ( d )
-- src:7179 | the number of days within which a notice of intention to contest or not contest is to be filed and served under Order 6, Rule 6; and
-- src:7180 | ( e )
-- src:7181 | a statement of claim or, if the statement of claim is not endorsed on the originating claim, a concise statement of the nature of the claim made or the relief or remedy required in the action.
-- src:7182 | (4) The address for service of the Authority is — ( a )
@ref O 62 r 2(3) (src:7172-7182)
GIVEN endorsement IS A `o 62 r 2(3) endorsement`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`o 62 r 2(3) the matters the endorsement has not yet stated` MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (IF endorsement's `o 62 r 2(3)(a) states the provision of the Act contravened by the defendant or under which the defendant is liable for the payment of a civil penalty` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(a) the provision of the Act contravened by the defendant or under which the defendant is liable for the payment of a civil penalty"),
        (IF endorsement's `o 62 r 2(3)(b) states the address of the Authority` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(b) the address of the Authority"),
        (IF (NOT (endorsement's `o 62 r 2(3)(b) the Authority sues by a solicitor`)) OR endorsement's `o 62 r 2(3)(b) states the solicitor's name or firm and a business address of the solicitor` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(b) the solicitor's name or firm and a business address of the solicitor"),
        (IF (NOT (endorsement's `o 62 r 2(3)(c) a defendant is sued in a representative capacity`)) OR endorsement's `o 62 r 2(3)(c) states the capacity in which the defendant is sued` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(c) the capacity in which the defendant is sued"),
        (IF endorsement's `o 62 r 2(3)(d) states the number of days within which a notice of intention to contest or not contest is to be filed and served` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(d) the number of days within which a notice of intention to contest or not contest is to be filed and served"),
        (IF endorsement's `o 62 r 2(3)(e) a statement of claim is endorsed` OR endorsement's `o 62 r 2(3)(e) a concise statement of the nature of the claim or the relief or remedy required is endorsed` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(e) a statement of claim or, if the statement of claim is not endorsed on the originating claim, a concise statement of the nature of the claim made or the relief or remedy required in the action"))

-- src:7172 | (3) The Authority must endorse on the originating claim — ( a )
-- src:7173 | a statement of the provision of the Act contravened by the defendant or under which the defendant is liable for the payment of a civil penalty, as the case may be;
