-- src:7182 | (4) The address for service of the Authority is — ( a )
@ref O 62 r 2(3) (src:7172-7182)
GIVEN `the proceeding is a civil penalty action` IS A BOOLEAN
      endorsement IS A `o 62 r 2(3) endorsement`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 62 r 2(3) the endorsement states what the Rule requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the proceeding is a civil penalty action`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): rule 2(3) speaks of the Authority's originating claim in a civil penalty action
        IF count (`o 62 r 2(3) the matters the endorsement has not yet stated` endorsement) EQUALS 0
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a bare "must endorse"; QB: NOTHING (O 3 r 2(4)) / other: JUST FALSE

DECLARE `o 62 r 2(4) how the Authority sues` IS ONE OF
    `o 62 r 2(4)(a) the Authority sues by a solicitor`
    `o 62 r 2(4)(b) the Authority sues in person`
    `o 62 r 2(4) the Authority sues in another way`

-- (4): "The address for service of the Authority is (a) where the Authority sues by a solicitor, the business address of the
-- solicitor endorsed on the originating claim; or (b) where the Authority sues in person, the address within the jurisdiction
-- endorsed on the originating claim."
-- src:7182 | (4) The address for service of the Authority is — ( a )
-- src:7183 | where the Authority sues by a solicitor, the business address of the solicitor endorsed on the originating claim; or
-- src:7184 | ( b )
-- src:7185 | where the Authority sues in person, the address within the jurisdiction endorsed on the originating claim.
-- src:7186 | (5) The Authority must, on presenting the originating claim for sealing, file with the Registrar the consent of the Public Prosecutor referred to in section 137ZD(1), 232(1), 236B(3), 236C(2), 236E(3), 236F(2) or 236H(1), as the case may be.
@ref O 62 r 2(4) (src:7182-7186)
GIVEN how IS A `o 62 r 2(4) how the Authority sues`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`o 62 r 2(4) the address for service of the Authority` MEANS
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `o 62 r 2(4)(a) the Authority sues by a solicitor` THEN JUST "the business address of the solicitor endorsed on the originating claim"
    WHEN `o 62 r 2(4)(b) the Authority sues in person` THEN JUST "the address within the jurisdiction endorsed on the originating claim"
    WHEN `o 62 r 2(4) the Authority sues in another way` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): neither limb speaks of the Authority suing in another way; QC: NOTHING / other: JUST FALSE (a STRING cannot carry it)

