-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 4 -- default of notice of intention to contest or not contest`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- (1): "Where the Authority has not applied for any order apart from an order for a civil penalty ..., then, if the defendant fails to
-- file and serve a notice ..., the Authority may, after the time limited ... and (a) upon filing an affidavit proving due service ...;
-- and (b) where the statement of claim was not endorsed on or served with the originating claim, upon serving a statement of claim on the
-- defendant, apply to the Court for judgment".  "Where", "if", "after" and "upon" are conditions: unmet, the answer is JUST FALSE.
