    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): rule 8(2) speaks of "a civil penalty action"

-- (3): an order under Order 11 "is to be construed as not requiring the disclosure of any document the withholding of which is
-- authorised or required under any written law or rule of law on the ground that its disclosure would be injurious to the public interest".
-- src:7217 | (3) Any order of the Court made under Order 11 is to be construed as not requiring the disclosure of any document the withholding of which is authorised or required under any written law or rule of law on the ground that its disclosure would be injurious to the public interest.
-- src:7218 | (4) The Authority may be ordered to give production of or produce for inspection under Order 11 the following documents which are or have been in the Authority’s possession, custody or power as a result of the performance or exercise by the Authority of any of its functions, duties or powers under the Act: ( a )
@ref O 62 r 8(3) (src:7217-7218)
GIVEN `the order was made under Order 11` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the withholding of the document is authorised or required under a written law or rule of law on the ground that its disclosure would be injurious to the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 62 r 8(3) the order requires disclosure of the document` MEANS
    IF `the order was made under Order 11` AND `the withholding of the document is authorised or required under a written law or rule of law on the ground that its disclosure would be injurious to the public interest`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is to be construed as not requiring the disclosure of any document the withholding of which is authorised or required under any written law or rule of law on the ground that its disclosure would be injurious to the public interest"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): rule 8(3) construes an order under Order 11 in respect of a document whose withholding is authorised or required on the public-interest ground, and says nothing of any other order or document

-- (4): the first list of documents.
DECLARE `o 62 r 8(4) kind of document` IS ONE OF
    `o 62 r 8(4)(a) a book voluntarily produced by the defendant or contravening person to the Authority`
    `o 62 r 8(4)(b) a book produced by or seized from any person pursuant to section 163, 163A or 164`
    `o 62 r 8(4)(c) an acknowledgment of receipt issued by the Authority for a book referred to in (a) or (b)`
    `o 62 r 8(4)(d) correspondence between the Authority or its solicitors and the defendant or contravening person, or their agents or solicitors`
    `o 62 r 8(4)(e) an examination requirement served on the defendant or contravening person pursuant to section 154`
    `o 62 r 8(4)(f) a production requirement served on the defendant or contravening person pursuant to section 163`
    `o 62 r 8(4)(g) a written notice or written production requirement in respect of the premises pursuant to section 163A`
    `o 62 r 8(4)(h) a warrant issued in respect of the premises pursuant to section 164`
    `o 62 r 8(4)(i) a written record made pursuant to section 158 of statements made to the Authority`
    `o 62 r 8(4)(j) trading information relating to the trading activities which the Authority relies on or will rely on in the action`
    `o 62 r 8(4)(k) any other document which the Authority relies on or will rely on in the action`
    `o 62 r 8(4) a document of another kind`

