-- (6): the excluded descriptions.
DECLARE `o 62 r 8(6) description` IS ONE OF
    `o 62 r 8(6)(a) a document in the Authority's possession, custody or power as a result of its supervisory functions, duties or powers under a written law other than the Act`
    `o 62 r 8(6)(b) a complaint or request received by the Authority to investigate or provide assistance on a possible or alleged contravention of the Act, or a similar document received by the Authority`
    `o 62 r 8(6)(c) the Authority's internal books`
    `o 62 r 8(6)(d) correspondence between the Authority and the Government or a statutory body`
    `o 62 r 8(6)(e) a document sent by the Authority to the Government or a statutory body but not provided under section 168B`
    `o 62 r 8(6)(f) a document received by the Authority from the Government or a statutory body but not referred to in paragraph (5)`
    `o 62 r 8(6)(g)(i) correspondence between the Authority and an overseas regulatory authority`
    `o 62 r 8(6)(g)(ii) correspondence between the Authority and a securities exchange, futures exchange or clearing house`
    `o 62 r 8(6)(g)(iii) correspondence between the Authority and the complainant`
    `o 62 r 8(6) none of these descriptions`

-- "The Authority may not be ordered to give production ... any document apart from those listed in paragraphs (4) and (5) unless the
-- Court is of the opinion that there are strong and exceptional grounds ..., except that no order may be made in respect of a document
-- falling within any of the following descriptions".  The exclusion is read as flat: it bars an order even for a document that is also
-- listed in (4) or (5).  FORK: the "except that" bars an order for a described document whether or not the document is also listed in (4) or (5)
-- (so the Authority's internal book that it relies on, (4)(k) and (6)(c) together, is barred): the exclusion is worded "a document" and not
-- "a document apart from those listed", and (6)(f) carves paragraph (5) out of itself by name, which would be surplus if the "except that" could
-- not reach a listed document / other: a listed document is reachable, because the sentence is about documents "apart from those listed in
-- paragraphs (4) and (5)" and the "except that" is an exception to the "unless" limb of that sentence, so it takes away the strong-grounds route
-- for a described unlisted document and leaves (4) and (5) alone ("may also be ordered").  Not listed: the bar of the "unless" limb (QA once the Court is of the opinion).
-- src:7267 | (6) The Authority may not be ordered to give production of or produce for inspection under Order 11 any document apart from those listed in paragraphs (4) and (5) unless the Court is of the opinion that there are strong and exceptional grounds to order the Authority to give production of or produce for inspection such document, except that no order may be made in respect of a document falling within any of the following descriptions: ( a )
-- src:7268 | documents which are or have been in the Authority’s possession, custody or power as a result of the performance or exercise by the Authority of any of its supervisory functions, duties or powers under any written law other than the Act;
-- src:7269 | ( b )
-- src:7270 | complaints or requests received by the Authority to investigate or provide assistance on possible or alleged contravention of the Act, or any other documents received by the Authority of a similar nature;
-- src:7271 | ( c )
-- src:7272 | the Authority’s internal books;
-- src:7273 | ( d )
-- src:7274 | any correspondence between the Authority and the Government or any statutory body;
-- src:7275 | ( e )
-- src:7276 | any document which is sent by the Authority to the Government or any statutory body, but is not provided by the Authority under section 168B;
-- src:7277 | ( f )
-- src:7278 | any document which is received by the Authority from the Government or any statutory body, but is not referred to in paragraph (5);
-- src:7279 | ( g )
-- src:7280 | any correspondence between the Authority and — (i)
-- src:7281 | any overseas regulatory authority;
-- src:7282 | (ii)
-- src:7283 | any securities exchange, futures exchange or clearing house; or
-- src:7284 | (iii)
-- src:7285 | the complainant.
-- src:7286 | (7) Nothing in paragraph (6) affects the operation of the Evidence Act.
@ref O 62 r 8(6) (src:7267-7286)
GIVEN `the document is listed in paragraph (4) or (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is of the opinion that there are strong and exceptional grounds to order the Authority to give production of or produce for inspection the document` IS A BOOLEAN
      description IS A `o 62 r 8(6) description`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 62 r 8(6) an order may be made for the Authority to give production of the document or produce it for inspection` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (description EQUALS `o 62 r 8(6) none of these descriptions`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no order may be made in respect of a document falling within any of the following descriptions"
        IF `the document is listed in paragraph (4) or (5)`
        THEN JUST TRUE -- by paragraph (4) or (5), which carry the conditions on possession (S-L1)
        IF `the Court is of the opinion that there are strong and exceptional grounds to order the Authority to give production of or produce for inspection the document`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is lifted by the Court's opinion, and a lifted bar grants nothing; QA: NOTHING / other: JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may not be ordered to give production of or produce for inspection under Order 11 any document apart from those listed in paragraphs (4) and (5) unless the Court is of the opinion that there are strong and exceptional grounds"

-- (7): "Nothing in paragraph (6) affects the operation of the Evidence Act."
-- src:7286 | (7) Nothing in paragraph (6) affects the operation of the Evidence Act.
-- src:7287 | (8) In this Rule, “book” has the meaning given by section 2(1).
@ref O 62 r 8(7) (src:7286-7287)
GIVEN `the question is about the operation of the Evidence Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 62 r 8(7) paragraph (6) affects the operation of the Evidence Act` MEANS
    IF `the question is about the operation of the Evidence Act`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in paragraph (6) affects the operation of the Evidence Act"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): rule 8(7) speaks of the operation of the Evidence Act only

-- src:7287 | (8) In this Rule, “book” has the meaning given by section 2(1).
@ref O 62 r 8(8) "book" (src:7287)
`o 62 r 8(8) "book" the provision that gives its meaning` MEANS "section 2(1)"

