§§ `Rule 11 -- orders made under section 137ZD(3) or 232(4)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:7293 | 11. Where an order is sought under section 137ZD(3) or 232(4), or under section 232(4) read with section 236B(6), 236C(5), 236E(6), 236F(5) or 236H(4), the Authority must file the consent of the Public Prosecutor referred to in that provision.
@ref O 62 r 11 (src:7293)
GIVEN `an order is sought under section 137ZD(3) or 232(4), or under section 232(4) read with section 236B(6), 236C(5), 236E(6), 236F(5) or 236H(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 62 r 11 the duty to file the consent of the Public Prosecutor arises` MEANS
    IF `an order is sought under section 137ZD(3) or 232(4), or under section 232(4) read with section 236B(6), 236C(5), 236E(6), 236F(5) or 236H(4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an order is sought under section 137ZD(3) or 232(4), or under section 232(4) read with section 236B(6), 236C(5), 236E(6), 236F(5) or 236H(4)"

-- src:7293 | 11. Where an order is sought under section 137ZD(3) or 232(4), or under section 232(4) read with section 236B(6), 236C(5), 236E(6), 236F(5) or 236H(4), the Authority must file the consent of the Public Prosecutor referred to in that provision.
@ref O 62 r 11 (src:7293)
GIVEN `an order is sought under section 137ZD(3) or 232(4), or under section 232(4) read with section 236B(6), 236C(5), 236E(6), 236F(5) or 236H(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority files the consent of the Public Prosecutor referred to in that provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 62 r 11 the Authority files the consent as the Rule requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`o 62 r 11 the duty to file the consent of the Public Prosecutor arises` `an order is sought under section 137ZD(3) or 232(4), or under section 232(4) read with section 236B(6), 236C(5), 236E(6), 236F(5) or 236H(4)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty does not arise; QD: NOTHING, and the companion `o 62 r 11 the duty to file the consent of the Public Prosecutor arises` answers JUST FALSE / other: JUST TRUE (nothing is unmet)
        IF `the Authority files the consent of the Public Prosecutor referred to in that provision`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a bare "must file"; QB: NOTHING (O 3 r 2(4)) / other: JUST FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 12 -- costs`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- (1): "Despite anything in Order 21, no order may be made for the costs of a defendant to be paid by the Authority where the Authority
-- discontinues a civil penalty action or withdraws all claims ... on the ground of the death or the bankruptcy or winding up of the defendant, ...".
-- FORK: the trailing "after the commencement of the civil penalty action" governs every ground in the list (the death, the bankruptcy or winding
-- up, and the commencement of bankruptcy or winding up proceedings), so the bar applies only where the ground arose after the action began / other:
-- it governs only "the commencement of bankruptcy or winding up proceedings against the defendant", so a death, bankruptcy or winding up that
-- happened before the action began is within the bar too.  The single input below is answered by the person on the first reading.
-- src:7295 | 12. —(1) Despite anything in Order 21, no order may be made for the costs of a defendant to be paid by the Authority where the Authority discontinues a civil penalty action or withdraws all claims made against the defendant in a civil penalty action on the ground of the death or the bankruptcy or winding up of the defendant, or the commencement of bankruptcy or winding up proceedings against the defendant, after the commencement of the civil penalty action. (2) Subject to the Rules in this Order, the Court may in or for the purposes of any proceedings in this Order, make such order as to costs as the Court thinks just.
@ref O 62 r 12(1) (src:7295)
GIVEN `the Authority discontinues the civil penalty action or withdraws all claims made against the defendant in it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on the ground of the death or the bankruptcy or winding up of the defendant, or the commencement of bankruptcy or winding up proceedings against the defendant, after the commencement of the action` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 62 r 12(1) an order may be made for the costs of the defendant to be paid by the Authority` MEANS
    IF `the Authority discontinues the civil penalty action or withdraws all claims made against the defendant in it` AND `on the ground of the death or the bankruptcy or winding up of the defendant, or the commencement of bankruptcy or winding up proceedings against the defendant, after the commencement of the action`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no order may be made for the costs of a defendant to be paid by the Authority where the Authority discontinues a civil penalty action or withdraws all claims made against the defendant in a civil penalty action on the ground of the death or the bankruptcy or winding up of the defendant"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): rule 12(1) bars an order for the costs of a defendant to be paid by the Authority in the cases it names, and says nothing of other cases

-- (2): "Subject to the Rules in this Order, the Court may in or for the purposes of any proceedings in this Order, make such order as to
-- costs as the Court thinks just."
-- src:7295 | 12. —(1) Despite anything in Order 21, no order may be made for the costs of a defendant to be paid by the Authority where the Authority discontinues a civil penalty action or withdraws all claims made against the defendant in a civil penalty action on the ground of the death or the bankruptcy or winding up of the defendant, or the commencement of bankruptcy or winding up proceedings against the defendant, after the commencement of the civil penalty action. (2) Subject to the Rules in this Order, the Court may in or for the purposes of any proceedings in this Order, make such order as to costs as the Court thinks just.
-- src:7296 | (3) Where — ( a )
@ref O 62 r 12(2) (src:7295-7296)
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings in this Order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a Rule in this Order limits the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 62 r 12(2) the Court may make such order as to costs as it thinks just` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the proceedings are proceedings in this Order`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): rule 12(2) speaks of "any proceedings in this Order"
        IF `a Rule in this Order limits the order`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to the Rules in this Order": what the limiting Rule leaves is that Rule's (S-L1)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (3): "Where a legal officer of the Authority, who has been admitted as an advocate and solicitor under the Legal Profession Act; or
-- a State Counsel, appears as an advocate on behalf of the Authority and costs are awarded to the Authority, such costs include such
-- items ... as would be included within the meaning of the word 'costs' in any written law as though an advocate and solicitor ... had
-- appeared."  "Where" is a condition (JUST FALSE unmet); "include" does not close the list.
-- src:7296 | (3) Where — ( a )
-- src:7297 | a legal officer of the Authority, who has been admitted as an advocate and solicitor under the Legal Profession Act; or
-- src:7298 | ( b )
-- src:7299 | a State Counsel,
-- src:7300 | appears as an advocate on behalf of the Authority and costs are awarded to the Authority, such costs include such items, including fees for drawing, for getting up the case and for attendances, as would be included within the meaning of the word “costs” in any written law as though an advocate and solicitor who has in force a practising certificate, and who practises in a Singapore law practice, had appeared.
-- src:7301 | (4) Such costs must be in accordance with any scale of fees prescribed from time to time to be chargeable by advocates and solicitors and may be assessed in accordance with Order 21.
@ref O 62 r 12(3) (src:7296-7301)
GIVEN `a legal officer of the Authority admitted as an advocate and solicitor under the Legal Profession Act, or a State Counsel, appears as an advocate on behalf of the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `costs are awarded to the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the item is of the kind that would be included within the meaning of the word costs in any written law as though an advocate and solicitor with a practising certificate had appeared` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 62 r 12(3) the costs include the item` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`a legal officer of the Authority admitted as an advocate and solicitor under the Legal Profession Act, or a State Counsel, appears as an advocate on behalf of the Authority` AND `costs are awarded to the Authority`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "appears as an advocate on behalf of the Authority and costs are awarded to the Authority"
        IF `the item is of the kind that would be included within the meaning of the word costs in any written law as though an advocate and solicitor with a practising certificate had appeared`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "such costs include such items, including fees for drawing, for getting up the case and for attendances" does not close the list

-- (4): "Such costs must be in accordance with any scale of fees prescribed ... and may be assessed in accordance with Order 21."
-- src:7301 | (4) Such costs must be in accordance with any scale of fees prescribed from time to time to be chargeable by advocates and solicitors and may be assessed in accordance with Order 21.
-- src:7302 | (5) Costs awarded to the Authority in accordance with this Rule, when recovered, must be paid to the Authority.
@ref O 62 r 12(4) (src:7301-7302)
GIVEN `the costs are costs awarded to the Authority under paragraph (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are in accordance with the scale of fees prescribed from time to time to be chargeable by advocates and solicitors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 62 r 12(4) the costs are in accordance with the scale of fees` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the costs are costs awarded to the Authority under paragraph (3)`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): rule 12(4) speaks of "Such costs", the costs described in paragraph (3)
        IF `they are in accordance with the scale of fees prescribed from time to time to be chargeable by advocates and solicitors`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a bare "must be in accordance with any scale of fees"; QB: NOTHING (O 3 r 2(4)) / other: JUST FALSE

-- src:7301 | (4) Such costs must be in accordance with any scale of fees prescribed from time to time to be chargeable by advocates and solicitors and may be assessed in accordance with Order 21.
-- src:7302 | (5) Costs awarded to the Authority in accordance with this Rule, when recovered, must be paid to the Authority.
@ref O 62 r 12(4) (src:7301-7302)
GIVEN `the costs are costs awarded to the Authority under paragraph (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 62 r 12(4) the costs may be assessed in accordance with Order 21` MEANS
    IF `the costs are costs awarded to the Authority under paragraph (3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): rule 12(4) speaks of "Such costs", the costs described in paragraph (3)

-- (5): "Costs awarded to the Authority in accordance with this Rule, when recovered, must be paid to the Authority."  The duty arises
-- when the costs are recovered; compliance is the payment.
-- src:7302 | (5) Costs awarded to the Authority in accordance with this Rule, when recovered, must be paid to the Authority.
@ref O 62 r 12(5) (src:7302)
GIVEN `the costs are costs awarded to the Authority in accordance with this Rule` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the costs have been recovered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 62 r 12(5) the duty to pay the costs to the Authority arises` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the costs are costs awarded to the Authority in accordance with this Rule`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): rule 12(5) speaks of "Costs awarded to the Authority in accordance with this Rule"
        IF `the costs have been recovered`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when recovered, must be paid to the Authority"

-- src:7302 | (5) Costs awarded to the Authority in accordance with this Rule, when recovered, must be paid to the Authority.
@ref O 62 r 12(5) (src:7302)
GIVEN `the costs are costs awarded to the Authority in accordance with this Rule` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the costs have been recovered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they have been paid to the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 62 r 12(5) the costs are paid to the Authority as the Rule requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`o 62 r 12(5) the duty to pay the costs to the Authority arises` `the costs are costs awarded to the Authority in accordance with this Rule` `the costs have been recovered` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty does not arise; QD: NOTHING, and the companion `o 62 r 12(5) the duty to pay the costs to the Authority arises` answers JUST FALSE or NOTHING / other: JUST TRUE (nothing is unmet)
        IF `they have been paid to the Authority`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a bare "must be paid"; QB: NOTHING (O 3 r 2(4)) / other: JUST FALSE
